WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.940
Sengoku War God Musashi!

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.620
Goal!

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.710
Raimon makes a tie at last!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.320
Heavy Machine Soldier Baron was broken through.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:40.890
Coach...

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.600
Now this is the Raimon I know.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.350
What do you mean?

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.090
This is how it should be.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.080
Do you have another strategy up your sleeves, Aphrodi?

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.640
The score is tied at 2-2!

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.590
Will Kidokawa Seishuu come out victorious? Or Raimon?

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.540
Nishiki-kun is amazing!

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.180
Yes! Yes!

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.500
Now they're tied.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.220
Things are looking pretty good for us.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.470
Maybe at this rate...

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.230
Yeah.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.920
Nishiki-senpai!

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.210
Impressive as always.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.940
That's my real power!

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.890
The game is at our pace now.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:57.940
Let's keep it going!

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:58.900
Yeah!

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.030
They think they're so tough.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.660
It's still a tie. Don't rush into it.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.970
Rush?

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:08.290
All I need to do is beat them down with my Iron Horse Warrior Knight.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.440
Calm down. Raimon is caught up in their own pace right now.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.670
We have to hold them down with our teamwork.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.880
Just give me the ball, okay?!

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.690
The match resumes with Kidokawa Seishuu's kickoff!

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:28.440
So you're not going to give me the ball?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:30.660
Kamiya!

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:31.580
Izumi!

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.980
Taki takes the ball!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:34.830
Sousuke!

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:36.820
Here I come, Raimon!

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.530
Here he comes!

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.510
He's really pumped.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.260
They know they're in a tight spot.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.290
Sousuke, Izumi! God Triangle!

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.290
Okay!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.040
Sousuke!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.350
Out of my way!

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.780
A pitch-down obstructs Taki as he tries to advance!

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.120
I told you not to rush into it!

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.800
Are you trying to play this game all by yourself?

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:09.890
I'm the one with the best scoring power on our team!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.890
If you want to win, then follow through with me!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.310
What?!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.180
They're arguing about something.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:19.220
Well, it's only a good thing for Raimon.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.480
I wonder about that.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.240
Nii-san...

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.020
Coach, please bench my brother.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.430
I know that he's a good player.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:35.120
But if he keeps up this selfish playing, Kidokawa Seishuu will fall apart.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.730
All right, I'll switch players.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.050
I'm switching Kamiya out for Taki Yoshihiko.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.480
Yoshihiko, there's something I want you to tell everyone.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.770
Raimon gets a free kick, and Kidokawa Seishuu has changed their players!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.920
Kamiya is being benched for Taki Yoshihiko.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.340
He's Taki Sousuke's younger brother!

00:04:58.720 --> 00:04:59.950
Yoshihiko...

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.320
What's the big idea now?

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.060
Captain, I've got orders  from Coach.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.430
The next strategy?

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.590
Yes.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:17.290
He says that when you decide who should be making the shoots, don't lie to yourself.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:18.980
That's all?

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.090
That's plenty.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.760
What a load of crap.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.840
Nii-san, these are the coach's orders!

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.750
Oh, really?

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.270
If Kidokawa Seishuu loses, the Holy Emperor election will make a big move towards the revolution.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.280
Aren't you actually hoping Raimon wins?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:42.680
If I tried to lose on purpose just for the revolution, that wouldn't be any different than what Fifth Sector does!

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.280
I want to win this match.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.510
I want to win and find our own answers!

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.140
I'll keep appealing to Fifth Sector with my own plays, that's all.

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.680
I won't let you get in my way.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.810
The game resumes with Shindou's free kick!

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:58.800
Hamano!

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.500
Flying Route Pass!

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.940
Hamano and Tsurugi's skillful passing sends them into the enemy's side!

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:08.510
Izumi!

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.220
Again?

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.010
It's ours!

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.010
Kishibe!

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.040
The pitch-down obstructs Raimon's attack!

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.240
The ball goes from Kidokawa's Shimizu to Kishibe!

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.100
Let's go!

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.900
Hissatsu tactics!

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.590
God Triangle!

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.990
You're not getting through!

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:27.860
Yoshihiko!

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:28.950
Okay!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.310
Tobisawa-san!

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:36.110
Kidokawa Seishuu breezes past the pitch-down with their clever pass work!

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.380
That was close.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.320
Kurumada-san!

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:39.780
Yeah!

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.880
They're full of holes when they're like that!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.760
They need me there!

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:49.840
Yoshihiko!

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:53.760
I won't make it!

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.500
You're not getting it in!

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.800
Shove it!

00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.610
Nii-san!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.810
I'll be the one to make the goal!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.230
It's a loop shoot!

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.120
Shinsuke!

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.360
Ow, ow...

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.670
Shinsuke.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.170
You saved me there.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.130
Sangoku-senpai...

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.530
Those movements just now...

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:39.390
That little fella is pretty good.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:40.270
Yeah.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.430
They respond to the moment and help each other when in need...

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.020
That's Raimon's soccer.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:51.170
You pests keep getting in my way.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.000
Aren't you ashamed of yourself, Nii-san?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.910
What?

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.780
Look at this field.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:02.490
Everyone is putting everything on the line for this match.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:05.530
<i>You're</i>  the only one here who's thinking only for himself!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.080
Don't talk like you know it all!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.050
Nii-san!

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.100
Shut up!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.410
Hunter's Net!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.650
The team is a mess.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.950
Nii-san, get a hold on reality!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:30.980
Shut up!

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.980
I don't think you've got time to argue with your brother!

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.090
Captain!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:38.950
Kariya's pass goes to Matsukaze and then Shindou!

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.240
Nishiki!

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.450
Got it!

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:41.750
All right!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:42.330
It's a hat trick!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:44.380
You won't get us again!

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:45.860
I'll make it in this time too!

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.160
Don't underestimate Kidokawa!

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:58.540
Big Scissors!

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.970
Yamazaki and Ooisokawa steal the ball from Nishiki!

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.690
That was so close!

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.310
Guess we won't get that hat trick.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.040
Just what you'd expect from Kidokawa Seishuu.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.220
They won't let me score so easily.

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:13.690
Kishibe!

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.700
You've turned it into a good team.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.370
Kishibe...

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.340
But we'll be winning this year too!

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.340
Hissatsu tactics!

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.250
God Triangle!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:32.410
Kidokawa Seishuu passes the ball up without letting Raimon touch it!

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:33.000
Tobisawa!

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.180
Don't you feel anything when you see them, Nii-san?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.220
What're you trying to say?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.680
They're all doing their best to win.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.270
Are you just going to ignore their efforts?

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.780
Just shut up!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.320
This is your end!

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.170
Tobisawa!

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:52.990
Sousuke!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.590
Don't give #10 any free spots!

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:56.360
Okay!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.170
Nii-san!

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:13.560
<i>He says that when you decide who should be making the shoots...</i>

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.480
Don't lie to yourself, Sousuke.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.850
Go, Yoshihiko!

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:25.740
Shoot! Make the goal!

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:26.670
Nii-san!

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:30.900
Oh no!

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:32.850
Shinsuke-kun!

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.630
Jump in!

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:35.780
I get it!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.830
I'll just have to do it!

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:42.100
Rage Jump Defense!

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.760
Go!

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.330
Kaboom!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.000
Shinsuke...

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:54.860
Nice cover!

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.260
They're really keeping their eyes on the mark.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.720
It worked out somehow.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:10:59.260
Yeah!

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:00.930
Yoshihiko!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.930
The match isn't over yet!

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.590
Nii-san!

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.650
It seems he understood.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:12.760
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.190
This is...

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.320
Tsurugi, teach me how to play the card game!

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:21.530
All right.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:24.330
I strengthen my characters with my Coach card!

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:25.950
Incredible...

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.090
But how about this?!

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.620
As expected of you, Captain.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.330
Sword Saint Lancelot!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:36.630
I won't lose! Instrumentalist Maestro!

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.130
I'll be the one to win!

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.460
I did it!

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.970
Inazuma Eleven GO card game!

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.930
We'll be waiting for you at the movies!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.310
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.950
There's not much time left!

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.950
Will the match end in a tie?

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:53.550
Captain!

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:54.690
Tenma!

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.110
Go!

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.440
Blow past the opponent and bring it to Nishiki!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:03.320
Okay!

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:12.360
You won't get through!

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:23.800
Iron Horse Warrior Knight!

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:25.010
Tenma!

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.600
I won't lose!

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.800
Demon God Pegasus!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.970
All right, he's through!

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:52.740
Go, go!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.200
Nishiki-senpai!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.090
Sengoku War God Musashi!

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.760
Heavy Machine Soldier Baron!

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:22.320
Bushin Renzan!

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.210
Guardian Shield!

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:34.910
All right!

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.000
Goal!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.010
Nishiki makes in a hat trick!

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:44.280
There's the whistle!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:48.430
The match ends with Raimon's victory at 3-2!

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:04.030
I never knew losing could feel this mortifying.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:05.900
Kishibe.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.740
Kidokawa Seishuu will win for sure next time.

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:14.540
Raimon won't lose either.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.230
Nii-san, I'm sorry.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.140
I couldn't do anything in the end.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.560
Your shoot was good.

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.190
It's just that their defense was really strong.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:33.600
Nii-san...

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:40.400
I wanted to win this match.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:46.410
You all did well.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:48.150
But...

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:52.880
I'm satisfied as long as the team has come together as one.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:53.660
Coach...

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.560
Thank you.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:15:00.090
Thanks to you, we can see the path we're meant to take.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:05.080
Coach, did you know it would end up like this from the start?

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.840
I had faith in you all...

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.330
That your hearts would join as one at the very end.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.950
Now you know.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:18.710
The real crises come up unnoticed when things seem to be going well.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:23.860
That's when those who don't know the pain of loss drown in their power...

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.590
...and forget the importance of having comrades.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:33.730
Today is a new start for Kidokawa Seishuu.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.060
Let's put our strength together and reach for victory.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:36.910
Yes, sir!

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:58.660
Tenma, get a good hold on that ball!

00:15:58.660 --> 00:15:59.270
Okay!

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:01.700
We've got a good team here.

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:02.440
Yes.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.710
There's one concern I have now though...

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.010
I've started thinking about Raimon next year.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:11.330
After we've left.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.860
Sangoku-san...

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:17.940
Before, I didn't even have the freedom to think about the next year.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:22.250
It's probably because we're able to play our soccer as we want to now.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.410
I want to leave something for the members who follow after us.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.270
Leave something...

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:32.140
Like a legacy.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:35.150
The fact that we fought here with our blood and sweat...

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:40.150
It'd be nice if there was a way we could let the following members know about it.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.600
It's all right.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.020
We'll be sure to pass it on.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.320
Everything you've left behind for us.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:52.160
What I was concerned about is the goalkeeper position.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:56.220
Who will protect the goal after I'm gone?

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:57.280
Well...

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.420
I've found a possible candidate.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:03.120
Candidate? To be a goalkeeper?

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:03.960
Yeah.

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.500
He's got some good talent.

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.760
Are you thinking of Shinsuke?

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:17.190
He can handle it.

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:21.610
Huh?

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.040
What is it, Shinsuke?

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:27.090
The back of my neck feels kind of tingly all of a sudden.

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:28.400
Oh, well.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.270
Back to practice!

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:34.360
Now that's nostalgic.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:39.870
Makes me remember the times when there was nothing else in my head except soccer.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:45.870
And the genius game strategist Kidou Yuuto, now a coach...

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.790
The times have changed.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:53.240
Still, the world sure went in an unwanted direction.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:57.110
We'll get our soccer back.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.020
Yeah.

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:03.690
A prickly path lies ahead.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.190
I'll do one more favor before I go back to Italy.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.410
I guess it's never going to happen for us.

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:15.160
We never get used in the matches no matter what we do.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.520
And the guy who came in the middle of it all can use an Avatar.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.450
There's no room left for us to play.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.060
Talent is everything.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:26.290
Don't talk about talent so casually.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:31.000
Actually, Nishiki said something similar when we first met.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:32.770
Nishiki did?

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.370
These are yummy!

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:45.880
That good, eh?

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:48.310
Being Japanese is definitely about the rice!

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:54.760
I met Nishiki when I went to watch Italy's youth team one time.

00:18:55.770 --> 00:19:02.000
He had just dived into Italy and found out that his skills as a striker weren't cutting it.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.370
He was really agonizing over it.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:05.980
Someoka-san.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:09.100
I think I'll go back to Japan.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:10.900
I can't even take the food here.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.720
Turning tail and running away?

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:17.370
What do you think about converting to being a midfielder?

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.170
What's this all of a sudden?

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.700
I got this far because I focused solely on being a forward!

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:24.170
You're too focused on what's in front of you.

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:26.980
There are things you can only see when you take a step back.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.840
I don't understand complicated things!

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:32.390
Then just be quiet and follow me.

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:35.130
I'll raise you to be a player who can put up a fight against the world.

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:38.010
What do you mean?

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:39.730
Are you in or not?

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:45.160
I wouldn't mind.

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:47.630
Okay, then that's decided.

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:49.830
You're my disciple starting from today.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.330
In other words, I'll be your master.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.290
Master?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.370
You better be prepared for some rough training.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.760
Ever since then, he's silently pulled through his training.

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:07.140
No matter how hard it got, and even when he couldn't see any progress, he'd keep at it day after day.

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:13.160
He comes off as an easygoing guy, but it must've been really hard for him.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.240
All right!

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:13.160
Nice shoot.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.460
Sengoku War God Musashi was a result of all that.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:19.660
What I mean to say is...

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:22.990
As long as you keep working hard and believe you'll get results, things will work out.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:26.660
Someoka-san, why did you do so much for Nishiki?

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:29.140
I wonder why.

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:35.080
I guess I couldn't leave alone a guy who came all by himself to play soccer in Italy's youth league.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:40.300
The good thing about Raimon is how they help out team members who are suffering.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:43.710
I guess you could call it Raimon spirit.

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:47.140
Raimon spirit...

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:51.020
Back in our days, that club room was the symbol of Raimon spirit.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.890
But your Raimon spirit lies over there.

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:59.710
You're creating a new kind of Raimon spirit starting from that place.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:04.490
Bottom line is... the rest is up to you guys.

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:05.750
Yes!

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.180
Are you really going back to Italy?

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:20.490
Nishiki-kun will be really sad.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.690
My teammates are waiting for me.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:27.080
And it won't be any good to get in the way of Coach Kidou.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.470
You helped me out.

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:32.140
I'm thankful.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:36.620
Hey now, you're embarrassing me.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.330
And besides...

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:43.070
I'm sure you know already, but Holy Road is only going to get tougher from here on.

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.680
Do your best, Coach Kidou.

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:48.090
You too.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.350
Yeah.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:51.290
See you.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:26.790
What <i>are</i>  the Avatars?

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:29.880
Our revolutionary wind enters a new stage!

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:33.450
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 Miracle Of The Revolutionary Wind

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:35.390
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:47.900
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:23:53.630 --> 00:23:57.020
There are things you can only see when you take a step back!

00:23:57.020 --> 00:23:57.760
That's all!
